====
Libraries add the controls, registers, and processes to the home. Add only the libraries that the organisation needs:

[cols="3,4"]
|===
| Question | Library

| Do we need a full information security management system, for example for ISO/IEC 27001 or NIS2?
| Security response and compliance basics, information security management, and asset and risk management

| Do we need to manage the risks of our own assets, also without a full management system?
| Asset and risk management

| Do we run IT or cloud services ourselves?
| Security operations

| Does NIS2 apply to us?
| NIS2. NIS2 also needs the other libraries above

| Do we need the basic central controls for our products, for example for the EU Cyber Resilience Act?
| Security response and compliance basics

| Are we a team under an existing ISMS that already does the central controls?
| Leave out security response and compliance basics. Add only the libraries for the work that the team does itself
|===

A library has a button for each of its parts. A part can be the controls, which go to the central control register, the registers, which go to this home card, or the processes, which go to the process register. Click the buttons of all parts of a library. A part that has been added is ticked.

